  "implementation": [
    "The launch graph resolves only the assigned IL row using the server-owned specification track, then invokes the existing probeArtifact with only that track packet set. The automatic sibling remains in the source inventory, never in the artifact scope.",
    "Artifact evidence names the exact route, track, family and specification digest; JSON is regenerated using --json-only. Default --check still checks both JSON and Markdown.",
    "Final-verification translation retains an exact IL track/family binding. Missing, wildcard and automatic tracks cannot inherit the vacatur family at consumer, sponsored, generation or download admission.",
    "The IL download core requires current verification for consumer and sponsored jobs, checks route and matter against the job, and supports the sponsored participant-owned Briefcase binding. The IL route handler supplies protected current verification through existing readers and honors the unchanged consumer-delivery control.",
    "Assigned RCAP delivery verifiers import the focused IL contract checks. Existing worker and mobile HTTP tests additionally exercise both funding paths through real ephemeral PostgreSQL and filesystem storage, with unchanged specification-pinned PDF fixtures at the render port.",
    "The pre-existing packet-delivery-contract positive fixture used a retired Mississippi route and crashed at base. Its positive job-building case now uses exact Illinois; an explicit assertion also preserves refusal of the retired Mississippi route."
  ],
